  "result": "Perfect! All 186 tests pass. Here's the summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Updated `src/invoices.js`**\n- Added `applyVoucher(invoice, { code, amount })` function that:\n  - Only works on draft invoices (NOT_DRAFT error otherwise)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID error)\n  - Prevents multiple vouchers (VOUCHER_EXISTS error if one already exists)\n  - Returns ok(newInvoice) with invoice.voucher = { code, amount }\n- Updated `invoiceTotals()` to:\n  - Include voucher amount in calculations\n  - Return `{ subtotal, discount, vat, voucher, total }`\n  - Calculate total as: subtotal - discount + vat - voucher (clamped at 0)\n\n**Updated `src/errors.js`**\n- Added `VOUCHER_EXISTS` error code\n\n**Added 12 new tests to `test/invoices.test.js`**\n- Draft-only enforcement\n- Amount validation (negative, zero, non-integer rejection)\n- Valid voucher application\n- One-voucher-per-invoice enforcement\n- Voucher included in totals calculation\n- Voucher with zero value handling\n- Large voucher clamping total at zero\n- Immutability verification\n- Voucher with discounts interaction\n\n**Updated `HANDOFF.md`**\n- Documented applyVoucher function\n- Updated invoiceTotals documentation\n- Updated invoice object structure with voucher field\n- Added VOUCHER_EXISTS to error codes\n- Updated test counts (186 total)\n- Added voucher implementation notes\n\nAll 186 tests pass \u2713",
